Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 14:20:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Say on screen that every learner gets the whole corpus

Switching learner returns a list of the same length, because the model changes
what each activity IS for a learner rather than which ones they may open. With
only the chips moving, that reads as nothing having happened -- and reasonably
so, since the endpoint answering /api/activities?learner=L02 with all
forty-two looks like a filter that is not working.

The activity list now states the spread outright: "All 42 activities are open
to you. What the model changed is the level each one sits at: 28 at Create and
14 at Apply." For the TUT curriculum that line runs from 42 at Create for a
first-week learner to 42 at Apply for one who has finished both modules, which
is the demonstration in a sentence.

aria-live on the summary, so the change is announced rather than only seen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FSDM1Wo7WiT7h5vJNaY23D
---
 web/src/Activities.jsx | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/web/src/Activities.jsx b/web/src/Activities.jsx
index bbe7b7c..a3a83be 100644
